2026-11-17T06:43:15.2703124Z I wrote `src/allowance/spend.ts`, and `architect check` passes (types, rules, drift). I haven't run `architect prove --env local`, so the 9 evals and the three journeys are untested. I can't run it with the tools I have.
2026-11-17T06:43:15.2703902Z 
2026-11-17T06:43:15.2704023Z The handler does this:
2026-11-17T06:43:15.2704389Z - **Load:** it reads the allowance through `steps.load`.
2026-11-17T06:43:15.2705305Z - **Refusal:** if the amount is more than `limit - spent`, it logs why with `Effect.logInfo` and refuses with `AllowanceExceeded`, carrying the amount left.
2026-11-17T06:43:15.2706489Z - **Record:** otherwise it makes the move through `steps.record(move(...))`. The move is `"exhausted"` when nothing is left and `"active"` when something is.
2026-11-17T06:43:15.2707191Z - **Answer:** it returns `{ remaining }`.
2026-11-17T06:43:15.2707398Z 
2026-11-17T06:43:15.2708857Z I'm not sure the move updates the `spent` field. The handler never writes `spent` itself, so the allowance may keep showing the old figure after a spend. If it does, `spend-twice-with-one-request` and `spend-within-allowance` are the journeys most likely to fail when you prove it.
